<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event · treaty</p><h1 class="enc-title">Auld Alliance</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1295–1560</span> · Also known as Franco-Scottish alliance</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Auld Alliance was the alliance between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>, first sealed by a treaty of 1295 between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-balliol">John Balliol</a> and Philip IV and renewed by most later Scottish kings. It drew Scotland into repeated wars with England, including the invasion that ended at Flodden in 1513, and brought French troops and influence into Scotland. It effectively ended with the Treaty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edinburgh">Edinburgh</a> and the Scottish <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protestant-reformation">Reformation</a> of 1560.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/auld-alliance.jpg" alt="Auld Alliance" width="320" height="249" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Joan Blaeu · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Atlas_Van_der_Hagen-KW1049B11_038-SCOTIA_REGNUM_cum_insulis_adjacentibus.jpeg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
